<article class="env-corollary" id="8A93C6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/8A93C6">Corollary <span data-tag="8A93C6">3.3.1.4</span>.</a> Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { X \ar [r] \ar [d] &amp;  X' \ar [d]^{p'} \\ S \ar [r] &amp;  S' } \]
</div>
  <p> be a pullback diagram of simplicial sets, where $p'$ is a Cartesian fibration. Then the diagram is homotopy Cartesian (with respect to the Joyal model structure). </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a categorical equivalence $S' \rightarrow S''$, where $S''$ is an $\infty $-category. Using Proposition <a href="/tag/AB6F70" data-tag="AB6F70">3.3.1.1</a>, we may assume without loss of generality that $X' \simeq X'' \times _{S''} S'$, where $X'' \rightarrow S''$ is a Cartesian fibration. Now choose a factorization 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  S \stackrel{\theta '}{\rightarrow } T \stackrel{\theta ''}{\rightarrow } S'' \]
</div>
    <p>
       where $\theta '$ is a categorical equivalence and $\theta ''$ is a categorical fibration. The diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  T \rightarrow S'' \leftarrow X'' \]
</div>
    <p>
       is fibrant. Consequently, the desired conclusion is equivalent to the assertion that the map $X \rightarrow T \times _{S''} X''$ is a categorical equivalence, which follows immediately from Proposition <a href="/tag/CAB1EC" data-tag="CAB1EC">3.3.1.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>